  "observations": [
    "Both compact compute modes produce severe false colors and structural hallucination in true T=1 mode.",
    "Original nonquantized BF16 weights also fail, so this observed failure is not specific to FP8.",
    "Real VAE-only reconstruction preserves the input colors and structure; the failure appears in diffusion restoration rather than ordinary VAE reconstruction.",
    "Lower CFG and repeating the image to 5 or 9 frames with no clean anchors do not provide usable restoration in the tested cases.",
    "Marking the degraded image as clean blurs/preserves artifacts; pseudo-clean ends for 9 identical images preserve the degraded input, rather than recovering the quality seen with real video context."
  ],
  "interpretation": "A valid tensor shape and changed pixels are not successful restoration. Same seed across different temporal shapes does not ensure corresponding noise. Video comparison also changes temporal context and clean anchors, so no single causal factor is isolated. No clean ground truth image is available.",
